TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT(1)       User Commands       TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.mailbot - IMAP/sendmail transport adapter for ttychatter

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.mailbot --once [--dry-run]
    ttychatter.mailbot --daemon [--dry-run]
    ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates
    ttychatter.mailbot --doctor
    ttychatter.mailbot --config
    ttychatter.mailbot --set KEY VALUE
    ttychatter.mailbot --unset KEY
    ttychatter.mailbot --set-imap-password [--gpg]
    ttychatter.mailbot --set-smtp-password [--gpg]
    ttychatter.mailbot --version
    ttychatter.mailbot --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.mailbot reads unread mail from an IMAP mailbox, selects messages
    whose subject contains tc:{session}, sends their body and attachments to a
    configured ttychatter command, and replies by sendmail or SMTP.

    The mailbot does not speak OpenRouter itself. It is a transport adapter:

        email -> ttychatter -> email reply

    This keeps provider/session/model behavior centralized in ttychatter.

SUBJECT FORMAT
    Normal chat request:

        tc:{session-name}

    New timestamped session:

        tc:{new}

    Configuration request/update:

        tc:{CONFIG}

IMAP SAFETY
    ttychatter.mailbot inspects unread candidates using IMAP BODY.PEEK[]. This
    is important: ordinary RFC822/BODY fetches may set the \Seen flag. Dry-run,
    candidate listing, skipped messages, and config inspection are designed not
    to consume unread state.

    A matching message is marked seen only after a successful real processing
    run, and only if MARK_SEEN is enabled.

ALLOWLIST BEHAVIOR
    ALLOWED_FROM is the main mailbot safety gate. It may contain one address,
    comma-separated addresses, semicolon-separated addresses, or whitespace-
    separated addresses. Matching is case-insensitive after parsing the From
    header to a bare address.

    A wildcard value of * is accepted for temporary local testing, but should not
    be left in production because anyone who can mail the bot could spend API
    credits.

CONFIGURATION BY EMAIL
    A message from ALLOWED_FROM with subject:

        tc:{CONFIG}

    and no config attachment causes the bot to reply with the current config as
    an attachment named ttychatter-mailbot-config.txt. Plaintext password values
    are redacted.

    To update config by email:

        1. Send tc:{CONFIG}.
        2. Save and edit the attached config file.
        3. Reply with the edited config attached and the same tc:{CONFIG} subject.
        4. Run ttychatter.mailbot --once, or wait for daemon/cron.

    The bot creates a timestamped backup before replacing the config. Dry-run
    reports what would happen but does not write config.

SECURITY
    ALLOWED_FROM should be set and narrow. Mail from other senders is ignored.

    Config editing by email is only accepted from ALLOWED_FROM, and only from a
    plausible text attachment. Do not expose the bot to arbitrary public senders.

CONFIG FILE
    Default:

        ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config

    Common keys:

        IMAP_HOST
        IMAP_PORT
        IMAP_SSL
        IMAP_USER
        IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE
        IMAP_MAILBOX
        MAIL_FROM
        ALLOWED_FROM
        REPLY_METHOD
        SENDMAIL
        TTYCHATTER_COMMAND
        SESSION_DIR
        ATTACHMENT_DIR
        SUBJECT_PREFIX
        MAX_BODY_BYTES
        MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES
        PROCESS_ATTACHMENTS
        MARK_SEEN
        CONFIG_SUBJECT_TOKEN

COMMANDS
    --once
        Check unread messages once and exit.

    --daemon
        Poll forever using POLL_INTERVAL.

    --dry-run
        Show replies/actions without sending replies, updating config, recording
        processed Message-IDs, or marking messages seen.

    --list-candidates
        Print unread From/Subject/Message-ID values and whether each candidate
        matches or why it is skipped. Uses BODY.PEEK[] and does not mark read.

    --set-imap-password --gpg
        Save IMAP password encrypted with external gpg.

    --set-smtp-password --gpg
        Save SMTP password encrypted with external gpg.

FILES
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/smtp-password.gpg
    ~/.local/state/ttychatter/mailbot/processed-ids.txt

VERSION
    ttychatter.mailbot version 0.2.0
